            <ArticleTitle>Dual left anterior descending coronary artery: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>453-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of Type I dual left anterior descending artery (LAD) successfully treated by coronary artery bypass grafting including the long LAD. This rare coronary artery anomaly is of clinical importance in the field of myocardial revascularization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
